@startuml neural-kv-cache
' The KV-cache family (LayerCache / KvCache / SlidingWindowCache): its structure, its
' growth law, and the two traps a future integrator must know about. Drawn muted because
' it is scaffolding — no call site in the crate constructs any of these types.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/neural-kv-cache.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 2 in docs/components/neural/cache.md §5.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title The KV-cache family — structure, growth, and why it is inert here

rectangle "**CacheConfig**\nmax_seq_len 8192 · num_layers 12\nnum_heads 12 · head_dim 64 · F32" as cfg #90A4AE

rectangle "**LayerCache**\nkey, value: Option<Tensor>\nshape (B, A, T, d_h)\nseq_len: usize" as layer #90A4AE

rectangle "**KvCache**\nlayers: Vec<LayerCache>\nupdate_layer(ℓ, k, v)\npreallocate(B)" as kv #90A4AE

rectangle "**SlidingWindowCache**\ninner: KvCache\nwindow_size: W\nnarrow to the last W steps" as sw #90A4AE

rectangle "**ModernBertModel::forward**\nbidirectional encoder\n— never consults a KV cache —" as model #2E7D32

cfg --> kv : shapes the tensors
layer --> kv : one per layer
kv --> sw : wrapped
model -[#C62828,dashed]-> kv : **no edge exists in the code**

note right of layer #ECEFF1
  **update** concatenates along dim 2 (the time axis):
  Kₜ ← cat(Kₜ₋₁, k_new),  Vₜ ← cat(Vₜ₋₁, v_new).
  Memory after T steps, both tensors, all layers:
  **2 · B · L · A · T · d_h · sizeof(dtype)** bytes.
  Defaults, B = 1, T = 8192, F32 ⟹ ≈ 604 MB.
end note

note bottom of kv #FFEBEE
  **Trap 1 — preallocate is incompatible with update.**
  preallocate installs zero tensors of the //full// max_seq_len;
  the next update **concatenates onto them**, yielding an
  (8192 + t)-step cache that is mostly zeros. It would only
  make sense against a write-in-place kernel, which does not
  exist here.

  **Trap 2 — the defaults do not describe ModernBERT-base.**
  num_layers = 12 is BERT-shaped; ModernBERT-base has **22**
  layers (heads = 12 and head_dim = 64 //are// right: 12 × 64 = 768).
  Sizing a cache from CacheConfig::default() under-counts memory
  by 45%.
end note

note bottom of sw #ECEFF1
  **update_layer returns the pre-narrowing tensors** — the caller
  attends over the full history for the current step, while the
  //stored// cache (and seq_len()) is clamped to the last W steps.
  Memory becomes Θ(min(T, W)) instead of Θ(T).
end note

@enduml
